   "source": [
    "hybrid_retriever = HybridRetriever(client, \"HotPotQA_hybrid\")\n",
    "hybrid_retriever.create_collection()\n",
    "qrels_subset, processed_data = hybrid_retriever.index_dataset(\n",
    "    dataset.select(range(0, min(subset_size, len(dataset)))), corpus, qrels\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "5cf466fb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Hybrid retriever evaluation scores --------------------\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'ndcg@5': np.float64(0.9395205570958921), 'recall@3': np.float64(0.9244186046511628), 'precision@3': np.float64(0.6162790697674418), 'mrr': np.float64(0.9835195811939997)}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Hybrid retriever evaluation scores --------------------\")\n",
    "result = hybrid_retriever.evaluate(qrels_subset, processed_data)\n",
    "print(result)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "518dbc3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "[As expected](https://cormack.uwaterloo.ca/cormacksigir09-rrf.pdf), all metrics for the hybrid retriever are better than that of either the dense retriever or the sparse retriever. "
   ]
  }
